+# Changelog
+
+All notable changes to tally will be documented here.
+
+Format follows [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/).
+Versions follow [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).
+
+## [Unreleased] — targeting 2.1
+
+### Added
+
+- **`budget` subcommand** — `tally budget --month YYYY-MM` prints each budgeted
+  category alongside how much was spent that month and how much remains. Each row
+  is labelled `ok`, `warn` (≥ 80 % of budget used), or `over` (budget exceeded).
+- **Per-category monthly budgets** — default limits (USD) defined in
+  `tally/config.py` under `CATEGORY_BUDGETS`: food $600, transport $200,
+  rent $1 500, entertainment $150, other $300.
+- **Warning threshold** — `BUDGET_WARN_RATIO` (default 0.8) controls at what
+  fraction of a budget the `warn` state is triggered; configurable in
+  `tally/config.py`.
+
+## [2.0.0] — baseline
+
+Initial tracked release: single-file JSON store, multi-currency `add`,
+`report`, `list`, `export`, and `stats` subcommands. Amounts normalized to USD
+at write time (schema version 2).
